    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0530" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v22/pg502"/>

                <head>289. Telegram From the Department of State to the Mission at the United
                        Nations<anchor n="1" xml:id="d289-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-11-15T16:06:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15,
                                1957—4:06 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Gadel 81. Re West New Guinea. Following is decision taken by Secretary November
                    8:</p>
                <p>“Confirmed that the U.S. policy of ‘neutrality’ should be continued on the issue
                    of West New Guinea, as to sponsorship, lobbying and voting on resolutions.”</p>
                <p>Secretary’s approval of neutrality as to lobbying was supplemented by following
                    comment: “If, but only if, it can be done without becoming public, I would
                    suggest that we would not be heartbroken <pb facs="0531" n="503" xml:id="pg503"
                    /> if there were no two-thirds majority seeming to favor Indonesia’s
                    claims.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d289-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d289-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 656.56D13/11–1557. Secret. Drafted in
                    UNP, approved in S/S, and cleared in IO.</p>
            </note>
